  "construction": "Canonical lifted-product code LP_36^(2x3) of Zheng, Zheng, Jiang and Xu (arXiv:2607.28605, appendix example of canonical matrices): R = F_2[x]/(x^36 + 1), A = (A' | q_1) in R^(2x3) with A' = [[1, 1 + x^11 + x^29], [1, 0]] and q_1 = [1; x^8 + x^13 + x^16 + x^17], B = A^* (transpose with x -> x^-1). H_X = B(A (x) I_3, I_2 (x) B) and H_Z^T = B(I_3 (x) B ; A (x) I_2) with B(.) the 36 x 36 circulant binarization (their Eq. 5), so n = (3*3 + 2*2)*36 = 468; both binarized check matrices are 216 x 468 of full rank, so k = 468 - 216 - 216 = 36. Qubit order: left block (3 x 3 tiles of 36, tile index (j, t) row-major, position within tile last) then right block (2 x 2 tiles). The map (j, t, s) -> (t, j, s) on the left tiles and (p, q, s) -> (q, p, s) on the right tiles carries H_X onto H_Z, so d_X = d_Z and the Z witness is the image of the X witness.",
